## 6. Interpretation (0) {.smaller}

::: columns
::: {.column width="50%"}
$$
\begin{aligned}
\operatorname{\widehat{goutput}} &= -107.92 + 1824.02(\operatorname{size})\ + \\
&\quad 157.87(\operatorname{bimas}_{\operatorname{yes}}) - 262.08(\operatorname{bimas}_{\operatorname{mixed}})\ + \\
&\quad 0.79(\operatorname{famlabor}) + 1.04(\operatorname{hiredlabor})\ - \\
&\quad 0.03(\operatorname{urea}) + 11.09(\operatorname{phosphate})
\end{aligned}
$$

::: fragment
This first regression is in `level-level` form (without any linear transformation). Thus, interpretations are straightforward:

-  1 unit change in $x$ causes $\hat \beta$ unit change in $y$.
