## 4. Model re-specification {.smaller}

Estimating the Cobb-Douglas production function. Note, that $\log(\cdot)$ stands for a natural logarithm.

$$
\begin{aligned}
\operatorname{\widehat{log(goutput)}} &= 5.72 + 0.55(\operatorname{\log(size)}) + 0.12(\operatorname{bimas}_{\operatorname{yes}})\ - \\
&\quad 0.14(\operatorname{bimas}_{\operatorname{mixed}}) + 0.04(\operatorname{\log(famlabor)}) + 0.03(\operatorname{\log(hiredlabor)})\ + \\
&\quad 0.25(\operatorname{\log(urea)}) + 0.13(\operatorname{\log(phosphate)})
\end{aligned}
$$

